1
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:41,000
The American saga begins this summer.

2
00:15:10,000 --> 00:15:16,000
Horizon: An American Saga - Chapter 1 is a western,
drama film directed by Kevin Costner.

3
00:22:45,000 --> 00:22:51,000
In 1859, families discover the lure of the Old West as they
settle in territories from Wyoming to Kansas.

4
00:30:20,000 --> 00:30:26,000
Meanwhile, a gruff cowboy finds himself on the run with a
prostitute and a young boy after killing a fellow gunman.

5
00:37:55,000 --> 00:38:01,000
Hayes Ellison, played by Kevin Costner.

6
00:45:30,000 --> 00:45:36,000
Frances Kittredge, played by Sienna Miller.

7
00:53:05,000 --> 00:53:11,000
Trent Gephart, played by Sam Worthington.

8
01:00:40,000 --> 01:00:46,000
'Ellen' Harvey, played by Jena Malone.

9
01:08:15,000 --> 01:08:21,000
Marigold, played by Abbey Lee.

10
01:15:50,000 --> 01:15:56,000
Sgt. Major Thomas Riordan, played by Michael Rooker.

11
01:23:25,000 --> 01:23:31,000
Horizon: An American Saga – Chapter 1 is a 2024 American epic Western film directed and produced by Kevin Costner
from a screenplay he co-wrote with Jon Baird, based on an original story by the pair and Mark Kasdan.

12
01:31:00,000 --> 01:31:06,000
The first installment in the titular film series, it stars an ensemble cast including Costner, Sienna Miller, Sam Worthington, and Giovanni Ribisi, with Jena Malone, Abbey Lee, Michael
Rooker, Danny Huston, Luke Wilson, Isabelle Fuhrman, Jeff Fahey, Will Patton, Tatanka Means, Owen Crow Shoe, Ella Hunt, and Jamie Campbell Bower co-starring in supporting roles.

13
01:38:35,000 --> 01:38:41,000
The film follows several characters navigating life in the
Midwestern territories amid the American Civil War.

14
01:46:10,000 --> 01:46:16,000
Costner conceived the idea for an epic Western film in 1988, but it
languished in development hell for three decades.

15
01:53:45,000 --> 01:53:51,000
The film was finally confirmed in January 2022 with Costner as director, with an original plan to shoot the
first two films of an envisioned four-film saga back-to-back and release them digitally on HBO Max.

16
02:01:20,000 --> 02:01:26,000
Much of the cast signed on in August, with filming beginning
that month in Utah and lasting through November.

17
02:08:55,000 --> 02:09:01,000
The first two films carry a reported combined budget of $100
million, of which $38 million Costner personally funded.

18
02:16:30,000 --> 02:16:36,000
Chapter 1 premiered at the 77th Cannes Film Festival on May 19, 2024, and
was theatrically released in the United States on June 28.

19
02:24:05,000 --> 02:24:11,000
The film received mixed reviews from critics and underperformed at
the box-office, grossing only $38.7 million worldwide.

20
02:31:40,000 --> 02:31:46,000
The film was filmed back-to-back with a sequel, Chapter 2, which had its world premiere at the 81st Venice International
Film Festival, and was scheduled to be released in August 2024 but had not been released as of December 2025.

21
02:39:15,000 --> 02:39:21,000
Chapter 3 started filming in May 2024, while Chapter 4 is in development.

22
02:46:50,000 --> 02:46:56,000
The film explores themes of montana, indigenous,
brothel, new mexico, american civil war.

23
02:54:25,000 --> 02:54:31,000
The tone is emotional.
